  "body": "## Result and scope\n\nPR2393's two-target source-sharing handoff now has an exact answer for **P104 Y0 and Y1: 78 new helper lifetimes are necessary and sufficient** in its fixed-source-path, X-only monotone relay model. The two correction supports have 48 entries each and share 18. A reversible two-total basis in their common frame lets those 18 source acquisitions serve both targets, with all arbitrary dirty inputs restored.\n\nThis adds only `research/p104-two-target-sharing/`: a written proof, literal circuit, source-bound receipt, a separately implemented mathematical audit, and a checked no-sharing comparison. Contribution head `6def43ad673b91dbd491389964d1dcd059bf2ac2`; scientific base `0fdd7d82de03e43c9e5a1000dfbcd380d1b687d2`.\n\n| Added quantity | Shared construction | Literal independent-entry comparison |\n| --- | ---: | ---: |\n| Helper lifetimes | **78** | 96 |\n| ZERO-to-FULL boundary rank mass | **702** | 864 |\n| Scalar ADDs | 440 | **384** |\n| Nested transports | **236** | 288 |\n| Source reads | **156** | 192 |\n\nThe shared word saves 18 helper lifetimes and 162 boundary rank units, while using 56 more scalar additions. Its added profile is `142 H1 + 16 H2 + 18 H6 + 60 H7`. The full partial channel has 4,734 events and 358 independent input columns. Y0/Y1 finish as identity transfers; the other 102 target rows keep the original G/2 channel. All original and added dirty helper logical values restore.\n\nThe lower bound is a written arbitrary-length dependence-path argument, with all 96 required source/target escape premises checked exactly. Rank-mass sharpness additionally requires every new lifetime to run ZERO to FULL with dimension-gap billing. It is neither a simultaneous physical-stock lower bound nor an excess-cost invoice. The particular ADD count and histogram are not asserted optimal.\n\n**No full supplier or new kappa.** Native phases/new scalar-address lowering, reverse-orientation admission, global owners and idle/residual children, the other 102 corrections, physical precision/tape and all-size admission remain open. The original channel's native proof does not admit these new transports automatically. The exact ideal logical prefix l1 maximum 106 and denominator 4 are not a roundoff proof. Selected/frontier records and frozen predecessor sources are unchanged.\n\n## Verification\n\nOn CPython 3.12, standard library:\n\n```sh\npython3.12 -B scripts/research_package.py --package research/p104-two-target-sharing\nmake selected-record-check\n```\n\nBoth pass. Registered replay checks sparse Fraction and separate dense dyadic integer implementations, all 128,164 endpoint coefficients, the original 280-column channel, the 376-column comparison,11 primary and7 independent rejecting controls, equivalent-basis positive controls, and both complete regenerated JSON payloads. Seven behavioral groups cover read-only Git-free execution, missing/changed evidence, source drift, malformed JSON, exclusive output, and sensitivity to deliberately removing the endpoint predicate. Final package bytes were replayed after formatting the literal events for review. Hosted CI is separate and not claimed passed.\n\n## Provenance, coordination and credit\n\n[Canonical advance claim](https://github.com/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/discussions/2245#discussioncomment-18946292). Main refreshed unchanged at 2026-10-15 10:18:36 UTC, priority revision 4; selected-record SHA256 `10b9e340fd8e354a37a0c4813c90e5de1dd42044b5f6aca4a3fc5a42b685fa32`. Submission overlap covered 644 open PRs including drafts at 10:18:46 UTC and 1171 Discussion records at 10:21:42 UTC, complete pagination and no warnings. It searches bodies/comments/replies and local README/TASK/ledger, not arbitrary code diffs; no match is not proof of novelty. PR2393's current head was rechecked unchanged.\n\nCredit commdata2338/PR2393 (`8b3e3a22c9e957990863ef60a561072dfcf08271`) for the one-target acquisition proof and explicit sharing handoff; Hiroki Kumazaki/PR2353 and Philippe Van Velzen for the relay model and lifetime distinction; Rohan Arun/PR1972, Chafik Boukhalfa/PR1991, Adam Gall/PR1940, Josie Elliston/PR1071, Ali Romman/PR1125 and the retained lineage. This changes the multi-target acquisition contract; it does not redo the pooled-space minima or the original-helper 41-contact lift.\n\nPrepared for Ross Richardson with substantial OpenAI Codex assistance in derivation, code, verification and writing, including a separate exact-circuit specialist audit. No independent human or formal-kernel review is claimed. Apache-2.0; predecessor notices and licenses remain. Next useful work is a named third-target collector-rank/chronology check or native admission of this exact word, as scoped in TASK.json.\n",
